#: ../../../source/Installation/Ubuntu-Install-Debs.rst:40
msgid "Steps"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Installation/Ubuntu-Install-Debs.rst:43
msgid "1 Set up your system"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Installation/Ubuntu-Install-Debs.rst:45
msgid "Set your locale."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Installation/Ubuntu-Install-Debs.rst:47
msgid ""
"Make sure you have a locale which supports ``UTF-8``. If you are in a "
"minimal environment (such as a docker container), the locale may be "
"something minimal like ``POSIX``. We test with the following settings. "
"However, it should be fine if you're using a different UTF-8 supported "
"locale."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Installation/Ubuntu-Install-Debs.rst:52
msgid ""
"$ locale  # check for UTF-8\n"
"$ sudo apt update && sudo apt install locales\n"
"$ sudo locale-gen en_US en_US.UTF-8\n"
"$ sudo update-locale LC_ALL=en_US.UTF-8 LANG=en_US.UTF-8\n"
"$ export LANG=en_US.UTF-8\n"
"$ locale  # verify settings"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Installation/Ubuntu-Install-Debs.rst:61
msgid "Enable the required repositories."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Installation/Ubuntu-Install-Debs.rst:63
msgid "You will need to add the ROS 2 apt repository to your system."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Installation/Ubuntu-Install-Debs.rst:65
msgid ""
"Ensure that the `Ubuntu Universe repository <https://help.ubuntu.com/"
"community/Repositories/Ubuntu>`_ is enabled."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Installation/Ubuntu-Install-Debs.rst:67
msgid ""
"$ sudo apt install software-properties-common\n"
"$ sudo add-apt-repository universe"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Installation/Ubuntu-Install-Debs.rst:72
msgid ""
"Install the `ros-apt-source <https://github.com/ros-infrastructure/ros-apt-"
"source/>`_ packages."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Installation/Ubuntu-Install-Debs.rst:74
msgid ""
"These provide keys and apt source configuration for the various ROS "
"repositories."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Installation/Ubuntu-Install-Debs.rst:76
msgid ""
"$ sudo apt update && sudo apt install curl -y\n"
"$ export ROS_APT_SOURCE_VERSION=$(curl -s https://api.github.com/repos/ros-"
"infrastructure/ros-apt-source/releases/latest | grep -F \"tag_name\" | awk -"
"F'\"' '{print $4}')\n"
"$ curl -L -o /tmp/ros2-apt-source.deb \"https://github.com/ros-"
"infrastructure/ros-apt-source/releases/download/${ROS_APT_SOURCE_VERSION}/"
"ros2-apt-source_${ROS_APT_SOURCE_VERSION}.$(. /etc/os-release && echo "
"${UBUNTU_CODENAME:-${VERSION_CODENAME}})_all.deb\"\n"
"$ sudo dpkg -i /tmp/ros2-apt-source.deb"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Installation/Ubuntu-Install-Debs.rst:83
msgid ""
"Installing the ros2-apt-source package configures ROS repositories for your "
"system. Updates to repository configuration occur automatically when new "
"versions of this package are released to the ROS repositories."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Installation/Ubuntu-Install-Debs.rst:86
msgid "Optional: Install development tools."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Installation/Ubuntu-Install-Debs.rst:88
msgid ""
"For building packages or other ROS development work, install ``ros-dev-"
"tools``:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Installation/Ubuntu-Install-Debs.rst:90
msgid "$ sudo apt update && sudo apt install ros-dev-tools"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Installation/Ubuntu-Install-Debs.rst:95
msgid "2 Install ROS"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Installation/Ubuntu-Install-Debs.rst:97
msgid "Update your apt repository caches."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Installation/Ubuntu-Install-Debs.rst:99
msgid "$ sudo apt update"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Installation/Ubuntu-Install-Debs.rst:103
msgid "Ensure your system is up to date."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Installation/Ubuntu-Install-Debs.rst:105
msgid ""
"ROS packages are built on frequently updated Ubuntu systems. Always make "
"sure that your system is up to date before installing new packages."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Installation/Ubuntu-Install-Debs.rst:108
msgid "$ sudo apt upgrade"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Installation/Ubuntu-Install-Debs.rst:112
msgid "Install ROS using one of the following methods:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Installation/Ubuntu-Install-Debs.rst:116
msgid "Desktop install (Recommended): ROS, RViz, demos, tutorials."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Installation/Ubuntu-Install-Debs.rst:118
msgid "$ sudo apt install ros-rolling-desktop"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Installation/Ubuntu-Install-Debs.rst:122
msgid ""
"ROS-Base install (Bare Bones): Communication libraries, message packages, "
"command line tools. No GUI tools."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Installation/Ubuntu-Install-Debs.rst:125
msgid "$ sudo apt install ros-rolling-ros-base"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Installation/Ubuntu-Install-Debs.rst:129
msgid "Optional: Install additional RMW implementations."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Installation/Ubuntu-Install-Debs.rst:131
msgid ""
"You can install optional RMW packages when your project needs a supported "
"DDS or Zenoh vendor other than the default. The default middleware that ROS "
"2 uses is ``Fast DDS``, but the middleware (RMW) can be replaced at runtime. "
"See the :doc:`guide <../How-To-Guides/Working-with-multiple-RMW-"
"implementations>` on how to work with multiple RMWs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Installation/Ubuntu-Install-Debs.rst:136
msgid "3 Set up your environment"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Installation/Ubuntu-Install-Debs.rst:138
msgid "Set up your environment by sourcing the following file."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Installation/Ubuntu-Install-Debs.rst:140
msgid "$ source /opt/ros/rolling/setup.bash"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Installation/Ubuntu-Install-Debs.rst:146
msgid ""
"If you are not using bash, replace ``.bash`` with your shell. Possible "
"values are: ``setup.bash``, ``setup.sh``, ``setup.zsh``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Installation/Ubuntu-Install-Debs.rst:150
msgid "4 Test the installation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Installation/Ubuntu-Install-Debs.rst:152
msgid ""
"If you installed ``ros-rolling-desktop``, you can try some examples to check "
"if the installation has been successful."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Installation/Ubuntu-Install-Debs.rst:154
msgid "In one terminal, source the setup file, then run a C++ talker:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Installation/Ubuntu-Install-Debs.rst:156
msgid ""
"$ source /opt/ros/rolling/setup.bash\n"
"$ ros2 run demo_nodes_cpp talker"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Installation/Ubuntu-Install-Debs.rst:161
msgid "In another terminal, source the setup file, then run a Python listener:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Installation/Ubuntu-Install-Debs.rst:163
msgid ""
"$ source /opt/ros/rolling/setup.bash\n"
"$ ros2 run demo_nodes_py listener"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Installation/Ubuntu-Install-Debs.rst:168
msgid ""
"You should see the talker saying that it's publishing messages and the "
"listener saying that it hears those messages. This verifies both the C++ and "
"Python APIs are working properly."
msgstr ""

